# Claude Code session state; /.claude/worktrees holds live git worktrees whose
# .git files would corrupt this repository if committed. Written as /.claude/*
# so the one exception below can re-include the committed project skills —
# git cannot re-include anything inside an excluded directory.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/

# SDD scratch ledger (session tooling, not project state)
.superpowers/
build/
release/
coverage/
.cache/
temp/
tmp/
logs/
*.zip
*.7z
*.mp4
*.mov
*.exe
*.msi

# Generated QA evidence
*.webm

# Blender automatic backups
*.blend2
*.blend@
# Design references and concept art stored separately.
# Written as /Designs/* rather than /Designs/ so the one exception below can re-include
# a subdirectory — git cannot re-include anything inside an excluded directory.
/Designs/*

# Exception: the pro-shop vertical slice is project-of-record, not concept art.
# SLICE_BRIEF.md and ANTI_SLOP_CHECKLIST.md are the permanent source of truth for the
# rebuild, and Designs/ProShop/Baseline/ is the pre-rebuild evidence that later phases
# are compared against — none of it is reconstructable once lost, so it is tracked.
# The baseline videos are the one deliberate exception to the *.webm rule above; they
# are a one-time ~13 MB capture, not recurring QA output.
!/Designs/ProShop/
!/Designs/ProShop/Baseline/video/*.webm

# Exception: the planning record and the feature slice briefs. ROADMAP.md is the single
# source of truth for scope — what the game is, what is in Property 1, what is cut and
# WHY — and a rejection whose rationale is lost gets re-litigated from memory. The slice
# briefs are the arguments behind it. All authored prose, none of it reconstructable.
# (FoundObjects and NamedGolfers were already tracked before this rule existed; naming
# them here keeps the intent legible rather than resting on index history.)
!/Designs/ROADMAP.md
!/Designs/Course/
!/Designs/NamedGolfers/
!/Designs/FoundObjects/
